Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Qore tree-sitter module packages
================================

This snapshot targets qore-testing. It ships native bindings, eleven language
parsers, upstream queries, compiler metadata, documentation and debug symbols.
There are no Qore user modules or app catalogs in this repository.

The package uses libtree-sitter >= 0.26.5 dynamically. Nine independently pinned
MIT grammar components contain their original source/grammar definitions,
queries and license files. No npm, Rust or network generation runs in the build.
The committed SQL parser is used directly without modifying the source component.
The Qore parser/scanner comes from the matching libqore-dev SDK. Built-Using
records its source package and exact version for source retention. All private
grammar symbols are hidden, avoiding interposition with Qore's astparser.

Prepare the module orig archive from a committed checkout excluding debian/.
Download the nine archives listed in vendor-sources.json outside the build, then
run debian/repack-grammars.py ARCHIVE_DIRECTORY OUTPUT_DIRECTORY. It verifies
checksums and creates deterministic orig components retaining only the listed
paths. Extract each component to its named directory without the upstream
wrapper directory; copy debian and run dpkg-buildpackage -S -sa -us -uc.
dpkg-source -x restores all components. Increment the version for each upload.

Build unprivileged offline with declared dependencies and the packaged Qore 3
SDK. Full, -B, -A, nocheck and nodoc profiles are supported. Cross builds fail
explicitly since Qore tools execute during the build. The query files copied to
the build tree are tested using QORE_TREESITTER_QUERY_DIR; installed tests unset
that variable and validate only packaged resources. Source-root changes and
sandbox denial on cached queries are regression-tested. Fresh qcc compilation
checks metadata, parsing and query execution without checkout paths.

Qualify source/component/query parity, debug/hardening, both default and custom
query roots, documentation, SDK-free install/purge/reinstall, all tests and byte
reproducibility across paths/job counts. Initially only Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 / SDK
.12 is qualified. Other releases/architectures, future upgrade paths and the
Qore ABI freeze remain general-release requirements. Testing PPA publication
requires matching published SDK/library dependencies, signing and upload.
